  <details class="cyq"><summary>1. You click "Run pipeline," it completes, then five minutes later you drag the "Max lag" slider without clicking Run again. What do you see, and why?</summary>
    <p>The exact same Results section as before — nothing recomputes. Dragging the slider triggers a rerun of
    the whole script, but <code>run</code> (bound to the Run-pipeline button) is False on that rerun, so the
    <code>if run:</code> block is skipped entirely. <code>result = st.session_state.get("result")</code> still
    finds the old <code>PipelineResult</code> and redraws it unchanged. The slider's new value only takes
    effect the next time you actually click <b>Run pipeline</b>.</p></details>

  <details class="cyq"><summary>2. Why does the Oil Volume panel use a session_state flag instead of just checking `if run_volume:` directly?</summary>
    <p>Because <code>run_volume</code> (from <code>st.button(...)</code>) is only <code>True</code> for the
    single rerun triggered by the click itself — Streamlit resets button state to <code>False</code> on every
    subsequent rerun. Without <code>or st.session_state.get("volume_loaded")</code>, the panel would render for
    one instant and then disappear the next time you touched anything else on the page.</p></details>

  <details class="cyq"><summary>3. If you wanted to add a "clear results" button, what would it need to do (in session_state terms)?</summary>
    <p>Set <code>st.session_state["result"] = None</code> (and probably the Oil Volume / microstructure flags
    too, if you want a full reset). Since the Results section is gated on
    <code>result = st.session_state.get("result")</code> being non-<code>None</code>, clearing that one key is
    enough to make the whole section disappear on the next rerun — no special "un-render" logic needed.</p></details>

